\subsection{NLP Finetuning Controls}
\label{sec:nlp_control_appendix}

Table~\ref{tab:nlp_controls} compares the two NLP finetuning controls used to test whether exit collapse is specific to action-oriented training.
Both chat-finetuned models produce completely flat action-probe profiles with $\Delta R^2 = 0.000$, confirming that NLP instruction tuning of neither backbone family induces the peak-to-exit drop observed in VLM-to-VLA transitions.

